    "result_text": "All green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: deterministic household identifier\n\n**householdId is now computed, not linked.** It's the first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`, so owners with the same last name and postcode share it automatically \u2014 no owner-to-owner linking.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- **`Sha256.java`** (new) \u2014 the single definition of the project's SHA-256 hex hashing. Extracted so `CustomerCode` and `Household` share one digest implementation instead of each rolling their own.\n- **`CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now delegates its `HASH8` to `Sha256.hex(...)` (removed its private `sha256`).\n- **`Household.java`** \u2014 rekeyed from *(lastName, address)* to *(lastName, postcode)*; `id(...)` now returns the SHA-256 12-hex-char value. Dropped the unused `matches`/address logic.\n- **`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 now just stamps the owner with its own deterministic `householdId` (only when it has a postcode). No repository, no member linking, no `sharesHousehold` check here.\n- **`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 the duplicate block now keys off the computed `householdId`: a second owner in the same household is rejected 409, **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set (which bypasses the block, creating a declared member).\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold`) is never flagged as a possible duplicate.\n- Javadoc/`openapi.yml` descriptions updated for `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, plus `IdentityKey`, `DuplicateIdentityException`, `AddressNormalizer` to match the new behaviour.\n\n### Notes on scope\n- The spec's \"household-size input to the membership level\" clause is vacuously satisfied here: this arm's `AssignMembershipLevel` derives the level from email presence and `namesakeCount` (first+last-name match), never from household size \u2014 so there was no household-keyed input to redirect.\n- `sharesHousehold` remains write-only/not persisted; `identityKey` is retained as a read-only display field but no longer drives duplicate detection.\n\n### Tests\n- `mvnw test` \u2192 **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0**, BUILD SUCCESS. The new `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` test passes (same lastName+postcode share the id; `sharesHousehold` bypasses the 409; a different lastName yields a different id).",
